meta {
  name: Match [Without Brand]
  type: grpc
  seq: 7
}

grpc {
  url: {{server}}
  method: /recordsimilarity.v1.RecordSimilarity/Match
  body: grpc
  protoPath: ../crates/similarity-proto/proto/recordsimilarity/v1/similarity.proto
  auth: none
  methodType: unary
}

body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "menu_item": {
        "fields": {
          "name": "Blueberry Indica Gummies 100mg (10pk)"
        },
        "quantities": {
          "weight_per_item": {
            "min": 40,
            "max": 40,
            "unit": "g"
          }
        }
      },
      "limit": 5
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  `recordsimilarity.v1.RecordSimilarity/Match` finds the stored records a menu item describes, best first, and says
  whether the best is the same product. A menu item is an entry on a retailer's menu: it names no stored record
  itself. Read-only: nothing is stored or changed.
  
  ## This request
  
  A menu item with a name and a weight and nothing else, matched against every brand's records (no `brand_id`), with
  at most 5 candidates and no `threshold`. Send `Import` first, so that there is something to match.
  
  The first of three candidates, and the decision:
  
  ```json
  {
    "candidates": [
      {
        "id": "bruno-import-1",
        "brand_id": "brand-1",
        "similarity": 0.94015,
        "search_similarity": 0.59460306,
        "fields": [
          { "field": "brand", "change": "FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED", "weight": 1.0 },
          { "field": "category", "change": "FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED", "weight": 3.0 },
          { "field": "description", "change": "FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED", "weight": 2.0 },
          { "field": "name", "change": "FIELD_CHANGE_MODIFIED", "similarity": 0.94015, "weight": 4.0 }
        ],
        "quantities": [
          { "field": "thc_per_item", "change": "QUANTITY_CHANGE_REMOVED", "previous_unit": "mg" },
          { "field": "weight_per_item", "change": "QUANTITY_CHANGE_UNCHANGED", "factor": 1.0, "previous_unit": "g", "unit": "g" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "decision": "MATCH_DECISION_NOT_JUDGED"
  }
  ```
  
  The decision is `MATCH_DECISION_NOT_JUDGED` and there is no `threshold` in the answer: the example config ships no
  match threshold and the request gives none, so the candidates are ranked and nothing is claimed about the best.
  
  The gummies score 0.940, on the name alone: it is the one field both sides have, and the three the menu item lacks
  are `FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED` and count for nothing. `search_similarity` is 0.595 for the same pair, which is why a
  match is scored again and not read off the search. The weight is the same on both sides
  (`QUANTITY_CHANGE_UNCHANGED`), and that is reported and moves no score. The other two candidates are the two
  cartridges, `bruno-1` and `bruno-import-2`, at 0.459 each. The scores are those of the default model
  (`mdbr-leaf-mt`) under `config.example.toml`; another model or other weights give other numbers.
  
  ## Request (`MatchRequest`)
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Values |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `menu_item` | `Record` | yes | The menu item, under the field and quantity names of the server's schema. See below. |
  | `limit` | uint32 | no | How many candidates to return, 1 to 100. Left out or 0: 5. |
  | `brand_id` | string | no | Only consider records of this brand, when the caller knows which brand the menu item is of. Compared exactly. Not blank. Left out: every brand's records are candidates. |
  | `threshold` | float | no | -1 to 1. Holds the best candidate to this, in place of the server's match threshold (`match_threshold` in `Describe`). The example config ships none, because it has to be measured, so without this field nothing is decided. |
  
  ### `menu_item` (`Record`)
  
  Map the menu item's own fields onto the schema's names, and leave out one with no counterpart.
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Values |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `id` | string | must be absent | A menu item's id belongs to the system it came from. Present: `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. |
  | `brand_id` | string | must be absent | Present: `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. To match within one brand, use the request's own `brand_id`. |
  | `fields` | map of string to string | yes | Field name to text. The names are the ones `Describe` lists: with the example config `name` (required), `category`, `brand`, and `description`. A field that is left out and one that is blank are the same thing: no value. Runs of whitespace count as one space. Text beyond the model's limit (256 tokens with the example config) is not read. |
  | `quantities` | map of string to `Quantity` | no | Quantity name to amount. The names are the ones `Describe` lists: with the example config `weight_per_item`, `volume_per_item`, `thc_per_item`, and `cbd_per_item`. A quantity the menu item does not have is left out. They are compared with each candidate's and reported, and never move a similarity or the decision. |
  
  ### A quantity (`Quantity`)
  
  A measured amount with its unit: a weight, a volume, a potency. A single value is a range whose two ends are equal,
  and a caller that has only one end of a range sends it as both.
  
  | Field | Type | Values |
  |---|---|---|
  | `min` | double | The low end. A finite number, 0 or more. |
  | `max` | double | The high end. A finite number, not below `min`. |
  | `unit` | string | The unit both ends are in. Not blank. Matched without regard to case or the space around it: `G` and `g` are one unit. |
  
  These units are converted before amounts are compared, so `1 g` and `1000 mg` are the same quantity:
  
  | Measures | Compared in | Spellings |
  |---|---|---|
  | a mass | `mg` | `mcg` `µg` `μg` `microgram` `micrograms`, `mg` `milligram` `milligrams`, `g` `gram` `grams`, `kg` `kilogram` `kilograms`, `oz` `ounce` `ounces`, `lb` `lbs` `pound` `pounds` |
  | a volume | `ml` | `ml` `milliliter` `milliliters` `millilitre` `millilitres`, `cl` `centiliter` `centiliters`, `l` `liter` `liters` `litre` `litres`, `fl oz` `floz` `fl. oz` `fl. oz.` `fluid ounce` `fluid ounces` |
  | a share of the whole | `%` | `%` `percent` `pct` |
  
  Any other unit (`pack`, `each`, a misspelling) is accepted and never an error. It is comparable with itself and with
  nothing else. `Quantities` > `ListUnits` gives the table the server runs with, each unit with its factor.
  
  ## Response (`MatchResponse`)
  
  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  |---|---|---|
  | `candidates` | list of `MatchCandidate` | The stored records the menu item may describe, best first, at most `limit`. Equal similarities are ordered by id. |
  | `decision` | `MatchDecision` | What was decided about the first candidate. One of the values below. |
  | `threshold` | float, may be absent | The threshold the first candidate was held to: the request's, or else the server's. Absent if there was neither. |
  
  | `MatchDecision` | Number | Meaning |
  |---|---|---|
  | `MATCH_DECISION_UNSPECIFIED` | 0 | Not sent by this server. |
  | `MATCH_DECISION_NOT_JUDGED` | 1 | No match threshold is configured and the request gave none: the candidates are ranked, and nothing is claimed about the best. |
  | `MATCH_DECISION_MATCHED` | 2 | The first candidate's `similarity` is at or above the threshold. |
  | `MATCH_DECISION_NO_MATCH` | 3 | The first candidate's `similarity` is below the threshold, or there are no candidates. |
  
  ### `candidates[]` (`MatchCandidate`)
  
  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  |---|---|---|
  | `id` | string | The stored record's id. |
  | `brand_id` | string, may be absent | The brand it is stored under. |
  | `similarity` | float | The weighted mean of the per-field similarities over the fields both the stored record and the menu item have. This is what the decision is made on. 0 if they share no field. |
  | `search_similarity` | float | The score the search found this candidate by: what `FindSimilar` would report for it. The search under-scores a stored record that has more fields filled in than the menu item, which is why each candidate is scored again. |
  | `fields` | list of `FieldScore` | Read with the stored record as the baseline and the menu item as the record. |
  | `quantities` | list of `QuantityScore` | The same reading for quantities. |
  
  The server fetches more records than it returns (`limit` times `match_overfetch` from `Describe`, at most 1000),
  scores each exactly, and returns the best `limit`.
  
  ### `fields[]` (`FieldScore`)
  
  How one field of the menu item compares with the stored record's. `FIELD_CHANGE_ADDED` is a field only the menu item
  has and `FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED` one only the stored record has; neither is scored. `FIELD_CHANGE_RESTORED` never
  occurs, and `below_floor` is never set: a floor is a rule for revisions.
  
  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  |---|---|---|
  | `field` | string | The field's name. |
  | `change` | `FieldChange` | One of the values below. |
  | `similarity` | float, may be absent | Cosine similarity between the stored value and the record's, -1 to 1; for `FIELD_CHANGE_RESTORED`, between the field's first value and the record's. Absent for `FIELD_CHANGE_ADDED` and `FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED`. |
  | `weight` | float | The field's weight in the overall score. |
  | `below_floor` | bool | The similarity is below the field's own floor (`reject_below` in `Describe`), which rejects the record whatever the overall score. |
  
  | `FieldChange` | Number | Meaning | Scored? |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `FIELD_CHANGE_UNSPECIFIED` | 0 | Not sent by this server. | |
  | `FIELD_CHANGE_UNCHANGED` | 1 | The same text, ignoring whitespace. | Yes, as 1. |
  | `FIELD_CHANGE_MODIFIED` | 2 | Both versions have a value and the text differs. | Yes, against the stored value. |
  | `FIELD_CHANGE_ADDED` | 3 | Only the record has a value, and the stored record has never had one. | No: new information is taken on trust. |
  | `FIELD_CHANGE_REMOVED` | 4 | Only the stored version has a value. | No. |
  | `FIELD_CHANGE_RESTORED` | 5 | The stored version has no value, but the record once did and has one again. | Yes, against the first value the field had, so that a field cannot be swapped by blanking it and filling it in again. |
  
  ### `quantities[]` (`QuantityScore`)
  
  How one quantity of the menu item compares with the stored record's. Quantities are compared as numbers after unit
  conversion, and never move a similarity.
  
  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  |---|---|---|
  | `field` | string | The quantity's name. |
  | `change` | `QuantityChange` | One of the values below. |
  | `factor` | double, may be absent | How many times larger or smaller the amount became; for a range, whichever end moved more. Always at least 1, so "eight times bigger" and "an eighth" are both 8, and exactly 1 when nothing changed. Absent for `QUANTITY_CHANGE_ADDED` and `QUANTITY_CHANGE_REMOVED`, and when `incomparable` or `zero_crossing` is set. |
  | `zero_crossing` | bool | The amount moved between zero and a value above zero, so no factor describes the change. |
  | `incomparable` | bool | The two values are in units that cannot be converted into one another. |
  | `previous_unit` | string, may be absent | The unit of the value the record was compared with. Absent for `QUANTITY_CHANGE_ADDED`. |
  | `unit` | string, may be absent | The record's unit. Absent for `QUANTITY_CHANGE_REMOVED`. |
  | `beyond_limit` | bool | Never set by this call. |
  
  | `QuantityChange` | Number | Meaning |
  |---|---|---|
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_UNSPECIFIED` | 0 | Not sent by this server. |
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_UNCHANGED` | 1 | The same amount after unit conversion: `1 g` and `1000 mg`. |
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_MODIFIED` | 2 | Both versions have a value, in comparable units, and the amounts differ. |
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_ADDED` | 3 | Only the record has a value, and the stored record has never had one. |
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_REMOVED` | 4 | Only the stored version has a value. |
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_RESTORED` | 5 | The stored version has none, but the record once did and has one again. Compared with the first value it had. |
  | `QUANTITY_CHANGE_INCOMPARABLE` | 6 | Both versions have a value, in units that cannot be converted into one another (`%` and `mg`). Not a bigger or smaller amount: another kind of measurement. |
  
  ## Errors
  
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | `INVALID_ARGUMENT` | No `menu_item`. A menu item that carries an `id` or a `brand_id`, or does not fit the schema (see `Evaluate`). A `limit` above 100. A `threshold` outside -1 to 1. A blank `brand_id`. |
  | `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` | The embedding queue is full. Retry with backoff. |
  | `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` | The request carried a deadline, and the server could tell it would not be met. |
  | `UNAVAILABLE` | The vector store cannot be reached. Retry with backoff. |
}
